<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73221" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁλόκληρ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>complete, entire,
			perfect,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολοβός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				585b36
			</span></i> ; <i>uncastrated,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίχλαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.Com.
					174.9
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς ἱερέας ὁ. νόμος εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anaxandr.
					39.10
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				233
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Asin.</u>
				33
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. ὑγιής τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					44c
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diog.Oen.
					39
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. μὲν . . ὄντες καὶ ἀπαθεῖς κακῶν .
					. , ὁ. δὲ . . καὶ εὐδαίμονα φάσματα μυούμενοι</span>”
				<i>perfect, complete,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					250c
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. καὶ γνήσιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					759c
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ὁ. δέρματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Philops.</u>
					8
				</span></i>
			 ; also of evils, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. πήρωσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
					296
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ἡ ἀνελευθερία] οὐ πᾶσιν ὁ.
					παραγίνεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1121b19
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1126a12
			</span></i> ; simply, <i>whole, complete,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτεσιν δυσὶν οὐχ ὁλοκλήρ[οι]ς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1386
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. βουλευτήριον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					1027.12
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iv A. D.)</span> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. οἰκία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PLond.</u>
					3.930.13
				</span></i>
			, etc. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. κολλούρια</span>
			drug-pencils used <i>as wholes,</i> for insertion in cavities, <i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				10.23.1
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Erot.
				</span></i>
			
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαρτί</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				3.226
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				16.68
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				7.8
			</span></i>.</div>
